  "body": "The spec [states](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/tables.html#the-table-element) that a `table` element may contain either `tbody` or `tr` elements as direct children. It also [states ](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/tables.html#the-tbody-element)that both tags of a `tbody` element may be omitted in many cases. I think this means that any `tr` element that is a direct descendant of a `table` element could be parsed either literally, or as if it were in an implied `tbody` element.\r\n\r\nI've only ever seen it implemented as an implied `tbody`. [Example here.](https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?%3Cstyle%3E%0A%20%20table%20%3E%20tr%3A%3Abefore%20%7B%20content%3A%20%22%E2%9C%97%20no%20tbody%22%3B%20color%3A%20red%3B%20%7D%0A%20%20table%20%3E%20tbody%3A%3Abefore%20%7B%20content%3A%20%22%E2%9C%93%20tbody%22%3B%20color%3A%20green%3B%20%7D%0A%3C%2Fstyle%3E%0A%0A%3Ctable%3E%3Ctr%3E%3Ctd%3E%3C%2Ftable%3E) Also, for what it's worth the [HTML 4.01 spec](https://www.w3.org/TR/html401/struct/tables.html#h-11.2.1) does not allow `tr` elements as direct children of `table` elements.\r\n",
